Announcing...

NetHack-- 3.1.3!

The DevTeam snuck a new version of NetHack 3.1 out last week, just as I
was trying to finish the NetHack-- 3.1.2 patch...  Well, luckily, the
3.1.2 to 3.1.3 patch didn't change anything that affected my changes to
the code...

I'll be posting a patch to the NetHack 3.1.3 code to convert it into
NetHack-- 3.1.3; NetHack-- 3.1.3 adds about a dozen new artifacts, more
than half a dozen new special rooms, about 140 new monsters and a few
other nifty things.

However, if you have an Atari ST/TT030 or Falcon030, you can play
NetHack-- 3.1.3 _now_!  FTP on over to atari.archive.umich.edu or any of
its mirrors; it should soon be appearing in the Games directory... the
filename is nhmm31c.zip, and requires a fairly recent unzip (5.0 will
do) or ST-Zip 2.x.  Please don't bug me or the archivists; they'll get
around to it as soon as they can, and I don't have the time or resources
to be sending people copies of the program archive.

Those of you with other computers will either have to compile it
yourselves, or beg someone else to do it.  If I get a chance, I might be
able to build it for DOS and OS/2, but you really shouldn't count on
that... I'm very busy (NetHacking and massaging some other source
code... oh, and working... ;-)).

If you build NetHack-- 3.1.3 for any platforms, please let me know, and
upload it to an FTP site near you.  If someone wants to make the
NetHack-- code available for FTP, let me know.
